## Review after implementation or fixes

After an implementation or fix cycle, suggest 3 to 8 subsequent code review cycles, with a count proportional to risk, complementary focuses, and a completed continuation prompt. This range is a project convention; additional reviews require a user request.

Each cycle checks the current state and connected code, records findings with severity, location, and evidence, and reassesses authorized fixes using affected checks. Fixes within the same round do not reset the count. Finish with integrated verification and residual risks, without creating artificial cycles or claiming that a review count proves the absence of bugs.

## Dependencies and delivery

Check full and production audits. Investigate advisories and record known risk and available fixes. Passing lint/build does not mean a clean audit.

Checks are explicit commands. Git hooks, push blockers, and branch requirements are not defaults. Update this document together with scripts and rules that change.
